pve-wdcbalancer (0.2.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Recommendations can be applied: live migration for VMs, restart
    migration for containers, HA migration for HA guests, in a task with
    up to max_concurrent moves per node. Each move is checked again just
    before it starts.
  * Automation levels: with full automation the timer applies the
    recommendations within the threshold; per-VM overrides (disabled,
    manual, partial, full) and the container setting are honoured. No
    moves while Proxmox CRS auto-rebalancing is on.
  * Rules are mirrored into native HA rules for HA guests (node-affinity
    and resource-affinity, named wdcb-<rule>); hand-made HA rules are
    never touched.
  * Notifications for new faults and moves; move history with results.
  * CLI: apply, ha-sync; readable times in history.

 -- pve-wdcbalancer maintainers <maintainers@example.invalid>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 22:12:02 +0000

pve-wdcbalancer (0.1.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * First release: cluster load balancing that recommends moves.
    Scores every guest (CPU and memory demand from usage and pressure),
    recommends live migrations with priority and reason for maintenance,
    rule violations and load balancing (migration threshold 1-5), with VM
    and host groups, VM/Host must/should rules, keep-together and
    keep-apart rules, per-VM overrides, a placement explanation per guest,
    the Datacenter > Load Balancing panel, the wdcbalancer CLI and a REST
    API. Nothing is moved automatically yet.

 -- pve-wdcbalancer maintainers <maintainers@example.invalid>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 21:27:24 +0000
